{"byteLength":486,"contentHash":{"algorithm":"sha256","value":"b5a7ffc14835a88ad6afcf926eca46f9c9ae7511f4965c8d524411f0cc5ccb04"},"kind":"skillDocument","name":"references/stdlib/IOError.md","producer":{"build":{"commit":"5de2594ad523fba4f38fa63f7a1b306e8a23eb0c","dirty":false,"provenance":{"commit":"git","dirty":"environment"},"target":"aarch64-apple-darwin"},"name":"benitoite","version":"0.0.13"},"schemaVersion":1,"text":"# Benitoite.IOError\n\nStatus: standard, in the prelude. It can be used without `import`.\n\nRefer to its declarations as `IOError.<name>`, for example `IOError.message`.\n\nFailures of IO operations. The type `IOError` is built in.\n\n```benitoite\npublic function message(e: IOError) -> String\n```\n\nReturns a human-readable description of the failure. The wording may change between versions.\n\n```benitoite\npublic function kind(e: IOError) -> IOErrorKind\n```\n\nReturns the kind of the failure.\n"}
